Welcome to the club.  This is why Nethack and its descendents
stay interesting for so long.  Do you stay interested in easily
beaten games?

> How the HELL does one get anywhere in Slash'Em?

Notice that you went from asking how to win to asking how to
make progress.  HUGEly different questions.  The way to wim
IS to make progress from game to game.  When you die,
learn a lesson.  And the lesson is rarely about the exact form
of death.  You'll learn what corpses are poisonous and such
and that's it for the exact form of death lessons.  No, the main
lessons are asking yourself "What decision did I make a while
back that got me into that situation in the first place?"  Start
asking THAT question and learning THAT lesson and a few of
your characters will advance farther and descend deeper than
the earlier ones.  And that's how to win.  By learning strategy
the hard way.  Fail to learn strategy from each death and you
will no longer be able to get deeper each try.

And relish how hard the game is.  It's how it stays interesting.

Early strategy advice - Play vanilla instead of Salsh'em for a
while.  Ascend in vanilla then switch to the harder descendent.



